  "caption": "Quinn signed up for an ocean swim and doubled the training, then doubled it again, paddles and all. By week three the shoulder pinched with every stroke, and Quinn decided to quit swimming forever.\n\nSwimmer's shoulder is often a gradual rotator cuff overload, linked to training spikes, technique faults, a stiff upper back and weak outward rotators. You usually don't need to stop swimming completely.\n\nWhat can help: trimming distance and parking the paddles while keeping tolerable volume, strengthening outward rotators, rows and shoulder-blade muscles, improving upper-back mobility, and refining your stroke with a coach before building volume gradually.\n\nGet it checked if night pain wakes you, pain started suddenly, lifting the arm feels weak, or nothing changes after several weeks.\n\nOur Sydney CBD and Chatswood physios can help. Book via the link in bio.\n\nGeneral information only — not a substitute for an individual assessment.",
